WEBVTT

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.670
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.697
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:27.508
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:19.852
Captain's Log,
Stardate 53447.2.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.326
The crew's enjoying
a much needed shore leave

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.260
on the Norcadian homeworld.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.299
While I visit Pendari, a planet
in the neighboring system,

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.097
I'm leaving Commander Chakotay
in charge of Voyager.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.501
You may want to run a diagnostic
on the shield generators.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.630
It's way overdue.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:34.673
Consider it done.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.867
And don't forget to keep tabs

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.773
on Neelix's little project
in the Mess Hall.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.175
He's still trying to enhance

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.803
the plasma burners
in his stove?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.939
With some of Seven's
Borg technology.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.107
I don't want him accidentally
turning the galley

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.811
into an assimilation chamber.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.046
I'll assign
a security detail

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.645
to keep tabs on him...
unless you think

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.314
we need to take more
drastic measures.

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:54.383
And most important,
be sure to tell your Captain

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.791
when she's being
overprotective.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:56.954
I'll do that.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.964
Thanks again
for minding the store.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:02.033
Even the Captain deserves
a vacation once in a while.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.466
And her First Officer?

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.403
He's looking forward to putting
his feet up on your desk.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.602
Chakotay.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:14.078
Fun last night, wasn't it?

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.876
There's another match
scheduled at 1500.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.916
I've got a systems diagnostic.

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.746
Correct me if I'm wrong,
but you're in command

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:20.843
until the Captain gets back.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.319
What's your point?

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.412
Delegate.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.252
I happen to know that
Harry's free this afternoon.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.656
Lieutenant,
you're not suggesting

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.557
I abuse my power.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:33.430
Tell me that's not lunch.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:37.333
It's leola ointment
for my skin.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.870
What happened?

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.701
I was so excited to visit

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:43.936
one of those beautiful
Norcadian beaches, uh,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.570
that I forgot to take
my dermaline hypospray.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.944
I fell asleep...

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:52.347
under two suns.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.544
Ouch.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.717
A little more color
than I was hoping for,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.953
but it'll be a beautiful amber
before you know it.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.585
How's your shore leave been?

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:07.599
Well, we've spent the last few
days at the Tsunkatse matches.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.134
Tsunkatse.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:12.330
I heard some crewmen talking
about that during breakfast.

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.394
It's exciting...

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.270
a real test of
strength and agility.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:18.003
You should come to the match
with us this afternoon.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.135
From what I've heard,

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.873
Tsunkatse is
crude and pointless.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:23.108
Well, I guess we won't be
saving you a seat.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.274
What about you, Tuvok?

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.840
You appreciate the martial arts.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.146
I have other plans.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.278
There's a micronebula

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.912
approximately 1.6
light-years from here

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.319
on the verge of collapse.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.621
We'd like to take
a shuttle to study it.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:37.060
Ah. An away mission
during shore leave?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.622
Commander Tuvok and I don't
require recreational activities.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.826
The Borg wouldn't know fun

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.664
if they assimilated
an amusement park.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:47.038
It's your shore leave,

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.597
but try to enjoy yourselves.

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.074
That's an order.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:06.257
Here's the navigational
data you asked for.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.724
Thank you.

00:07:07.794 --> 00:07:10.729
How long are you
planning on being gone?

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:12.765
Approximately 48 hours.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.392
Just like B'Elanna.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.457
Clarify.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:18.697
Well, she overpacks, too.

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:20.636
I haven't overpacked.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:24.836
I simply wish to be prepared
for any contingency.

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:27.243
And what contingency
is this for?

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.905
That's an iso-modulator,

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:32.347
enhanced to correct hull
ablation in the event

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.716
we encounter
a meteoroid stream.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:38.086
Well, couldn't you just
replicate an iso-modulator?

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.488
I prefer this one.

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.083
Oh, I get it.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.253
You like to have your
own things with you.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:44.523
B'Elanna's the same way.

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:45.894
You know, she'd never admit it,

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:47.933
but she still takes
a stuffed animal with her

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.797
whenever she's
going to be away

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:51.029
for more than a day.

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:53.401
Toby the targ.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:56.931
Can Toby the targ
correct hull ablation?

00:07:57.076 --> 00:07:59.442
Your comparison is flawed.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:07.282
Just the person
I was looking for.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.581
You require my assistance?

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:09.586
Your company.

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.145
I was wondering if you'd care

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:12.282
to join me on a tour

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.121
of Norcadia's
cultural hot spots.

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:15.251
I hear their museums

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:17.228
are among the finest
in this sector.

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:18.228
I'm busy.

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:19.229
With what?

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.595
Commander Tuvok and I
are leaving

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:22.065
to study a collapsing
micronebula.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:23.726
During shore leave?

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:27.802
I thought we'd discussed this.

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.308
Shore leave is
a perfect opportunity

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:31.809
for you to spend time
with other members

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:33.709
of the crew to develop
your social skills.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.440
Then I suppose I'll have

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.380
to develop them
with Commander Tuvok.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:42.149
Vulcans aren't exactly known
for their winning personalities.

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:44.121
You'd prefer I spent my time

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.591
with more sociable individuals,
such as yourself?

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.924
You could do worse.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:51.223
In that case,

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:53.322
perhaps you'd care to join us.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:55.196
To study the micronebula?

00:08:55.268 --> 00:08:57.099
You can assist us
with our analysis

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.830
of veridium-oxide particulates.

00:08:58.905 --> 00:09:00.930
On second thought,

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:04.304
you and Tuvok have a good time.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:06.868
I'll give the Commander
your regrets.

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:08.072
Uh, do that.

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:10.615
And if the nebula
isn't as riveting

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:13.675
as you'd hoped,
try to remember Lesson 36...

00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:16.620
"Pleasant Parlor Games
to Pass the Time."

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:20.218
You'll need it.

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:36.905
Two hours, 37 minutes,
13 seconds.

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:38.806
That's how long we've gone

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.869
without verbal communication.

00:09:40.947 --> 00:09:43.507
Why is that remarkable?

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:46.916
The Doctor encourages me
to engage in conversation

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:48.578
during awkward silences.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:53.016
Did you find
the silence awkward?

00:09:54.627 --> 00:09:56.424
No.

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.395
Nor did I.

00:10:01.434 --> 00:10:04.096
There's a vessel approaching
on an intercept course.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.263
The hull configuration
is unfamiliar.

00:10:06.339 --> 00:10:07.829
Distance?

00:10:07.907 --> 00:10:10.375
Approximately
300,000 kilometers.

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:12.308
Hail them.

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:15.245
No response.

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:23.413
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:10:23.489 --> 00:10:24.717
The vessel is emitting

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.485
some kind of dampening field.

00:10:26.559 --> 00:10:27.685
We've lost engines,

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.058
weapons, shields.

00:10:42.675 --> 00:10:45.473
It's an explosive device
of some sort.

00:10:45.544 --> 00:10:47.569
Transporters are down.
I can't beam it off.

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:50.548
I'll try to disarm it.

00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:05.630
Borg-enhanced physiology.

00:11:05.698 --> 00:11:08.929
You should have
superior strength, agility,

00:11:09.035 --> 00:11:10.559
stamina,

00:11:10.636 --> 00:11:12.194
visual acuity.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.674
Welcome to Tsunkatse.

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:18.471
Since the game's inception,

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:21.069
our audience has never had
the pleasure

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:22.808
of seeing a
drone compete.

00:11:22.882 --> 00:11:28.946
You are going to be
a very popular attraction.

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:38.253
Where is Commander Tuvok?

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.491
Your comrade
from the shuttle?

00:11:40.566 --> 00:11:41.498
I'm afraid he was

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:42.864
injured in the explosion.

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:45.904
I wish to see him now.

00:11:45.971 --> 00:11:47.404
Certainly.

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:51.903
You'll learn nothing
is more important to me

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:54.377
than the comfort and happiness
of my fighters.

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:56.210
Yes, Penk's

00:11:56.282 --> 00:12:00.412
generosity is... legendary.

00:12:01.954 --> 00:12:04.616
Quiet!

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:09.491
He's envious because I've found
a new favorite.

00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:12.588
I have no intention
of participating in your game.

00:12:12.665 --> 00:12:13.927
Aggressive.

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:15.466
I like that.

00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:27.208
He requires medical attention.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:28.576
That can be arranged.

00:12:28.647 --> 00:12:30.638
Then arrange it.

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:31.944
You haven't won a single bout

00:12:32.051 --> 00:12:33.518
and already
you're making demands

00:12:33.586 --> 00:12:34.518
like a champion.

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:35.884
Will you treat him or not?

00:12:35.955 --> 00:12:37.923
Will you fight?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:40.356
Do not comply.

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:42.860
My condition is not severe.

00:12:42.928 --> 00:12:44.657
Spoken like
a true competitor,

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.527
willing to ignore his injuries

00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:48.123
for the sake of the contest.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.565
Schedule a bout for him.

00:12:49.635 --> 00:12:50.567
A Red Match

00:12:50.636 --> 00:12:51.933
against the Pensarkan.

00:12:52.004 --> 00:12:53.938
A Red Match

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:57.271
does not end until one
of the competitors is killed.

00:12:57.343 --> 00:13:00.335
Your friend would not survive.

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:02.141
But you might.

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:05.741
Give her a Blue Match, Penk.

00:13:05.818 --> 00:13:08.150
You wouldn't want to lose
your new favorite

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.881
her first time in the pit.

00:13:12.691 --> 00:13:15.990
Yes. We should
start you off slowly.

00:13:20.166 --> 00:13:21.929
Treat him...

00:13:22.034 --> 00:13:25.231
and I will comply.

00:13:33.813 --> 00:13:35.303
What about
the seventh match?

00:13:35.381 --> 00:13:36.848
I'm picking the Vensiddian.

00:13:36.916 --> 00:13:38.543
He lost his last two times out.

00:13:38.617 --> 00:13:41.211
But he's undefeated
against left-handed fighters.

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:42.845
You should trust him, Harry.

00:13:42.922 --> 00:13:45.618
Chakotay knows a thing or two
about southpaws.

00:13:45.691 --> 00:13:48.353
He was 23 and 0
as a light heavyweight.

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:49.917
23 and one,
actually...

00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:52.463
a Nausicaan with
a mean right hook.

00:13:52.531 --> 00:13:53.623
You think that's bad?

00:13:53.699 --> 00:13:55.462
Try taking a parrises
mallet to the ribs.

00:13:55.534 --> 00:13:57.092
I didn't know you played.

00:13:57.169 --> 00:13:59.603
Three-time Academy champion.

00:13:59.672 --> 00:14:01.105
Now, that's a tough sport.

00:14:01.173 --> 00:14:02.800
I boxed a few parrises players
in my day.

00:14:02.875 --> 00:14:05.469
And?

00:14:05.544 --> 00:14:07.171
Let's just say
they went back

00:14:07.246 --> 00:14:09.544
to playing parrises
squares after that.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.715
Oh, is that a challenge,
Commander?

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:14.218
I wouldn't want

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:16.686
to put my Ops Officer out
of commission, now, would I?

00:14:16.755 --> 00:14:19.315
Oh... I can take a punch.

00:14:19.391 --> 00:14:20.722
Careful, Harry.

00:14:20.793 --> 00:14:22.920
Legend has it that
the "Tattooed Terror"

00:14:23.062 --> 00:14:25.826
has put more men in Sick Bay
than the Ankaran flu.

00:14:25.898 --> 00:14:29.425
Yeah, you wouldn't want
to bruise your clarinet fingers.

00:14:30.803 --> 00:14:33.431
Hey, you want
to go a few rounds

00:14:33.505 --> 00:14:34.472
or all you all talk?

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.031
Any time, any place.

00:14:37.109 --> 00:14:38.974
Oh, you punch like a Ferengi.

00:14:43.749 --> 00:14:45.546
I don't care what Harry says.

00:14:45.618 --> 00:14:47.950
The Pensarkan-Bendali match
is too close to call.

00:14:48.087 --> 00:14:49.748
I'll let you know
how it turns out.

00:14:49.822 --> 00:14:50.948
Excuse me?

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.684
I rearranged the duty
schedules this morning.

00:14:53.759 --> 00:14:56.421
You've got the Bridge
starting at 1400 hours.

00:14:56.495 --> 00:14:58.122
You're sticking me
with that shift

00:14:58.197 --> 00:14:59.755
so that you can go to the fight.

00:14:59.832 --> 00:15:01.766
I'm delegating.

00:15:01.834 --> 00:15:03.802
Oh, me and my big mouth.

00:15:03.869 --> 00:15:07.896
I thought you'd be pleased
that I took your advice.

00:15:08.007 --> 00:15:08.996
Words fail me.

00:15:09.074 --> 00:15:10.098
Now, remind me.

00:15:10.175 --> 00:15:11.369
The reason that you have

00:15:11.443 --> 00:15:13.070
to see that fight
is because?

00:15:13.145 --> 00:15:14.840
I'm an anthropologist.

00:15:14.914 --> 00:15:17.075
What does that have
to do with Tsunkatse?

00:15:17.149 --> 00:15:18.616
It's a cultural phenomenon.

00:15:23.489 --> 00:15:26.515
You're having
an allergic reaction

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:28.719
to your leola ointment.

00:15:28.794 --> 00:15:30.625
I hope you've
learned your lesson.

00:15:30.696 --> 00:15:31.685
Talaxian homeopathy

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:33.789
is no substitute
for medical science.

00:15:33.866 --> 00:15:36.664
This should help with the
swelling and discoloration.

00:15:36.735 --> 00:15:37.793
Ow.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.565
But you'll have
to stay out of the sun.

00:15:39.638 --> 00:15:41.538
But what about the rest
of my shore leave?

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:44.269
I suggest you limit it
to indoor activities.

00:15:44.343 --> 00:15:47.312
Commander Chakotay
and B'Elanna invited me

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:49.142
to the Tsunkatse matches.

00:15:49.214 --> 00:15:50.340
I guess I'll go.

00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:52.316
I'm disappointed in
you, Mr. Neelix.

00:15:52.384 --> 00:15:53.942
Cheering for one individual

00:15:54.086 --> 00:15:55.917
to inflict
serious injury on another

00:15:55.988 --> 00:15:58.149
hardly seems like
an activity you'd enjoy.

00:15:58.223 --> 00:16:00.123
Well, Commander Chakotay
says that it's

00:16:00.192 --> 00:16:02.752
a wonderful demonstration
of athletic prowess.

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:04.125
You seem to be forgetting

00:16:04.196 --> 00:16:06.721
that Commander Chakotay is
an aficionado of boxing,

00:16:06.799 --> 00:16:09.495
arguably the most barbaric sport
in Earth's history.

00:16:09.568 --> 00:16:11.433
Surely you can find some way
to occupy your free time

00:16:11.503 --> 00:16:13.801
that doesn't involve
alien fisticuffs.

00:16:13.872 --> 00:16:16.136
Do you have any suggestions?

00:16:16.208 --> 00:16:18.699
As a matter of fact,
I was planning a visit

00:16:18.777 --> 00:16:20.904
to the Norcadian
Museum of Entomology

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:21.912
this afternoon.

00:16:21.981 --> 00:16:24.677
There's a fascinating
exhibit of beetle larvae

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.650
from the equatorial
subcontinent.

00:16:26.719 --> 00:16:28.186
You're welcome to join me.

00:16:28.253 --> 00:16:32.815
Hmm, alien bugs
or alien fisticuffs.

00:16:32.891 --> 00:16:35.018
Oh, that's a tough one.

00:16:35.127 --> 00:16:37.118
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:16:46.071 --> 00:16:48.369
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:52.376
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:17:06.291 --> 00:17:07.883
You were right, Commander.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:08.984
This is exciting.

00:17:09.061 --> 00:17:10.221
Two opponents alone

00:17:10.295 --> 00:17:11.887
in the pit with
only their strength

00:17:11.964 --> 00:17:13.454
and agility to protect them.

00:17:13.532 --> 00:17:15.898
I'm glad
you're enjoying yourself.

00:17:15.968 --> 00:17:17.367
I still don't understand
the rules.

00:17:17.436 --> 00:17:18.835
It's simple.

00:17:18.904 --> 00:17:21.600
A Tsunkatse fighter wears
a polaron disruptor on both

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:23.698
hands and feet.
Each disruptor delivers

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:26.609
a bioplasmic charge
when it comes in contact with

00:17:26.678 --> 00:17:28.270
one of the opponent's
target sensors.

00:17:28.347 --> 00:17:29.678
So there is strategy involved.

00:17:29.748 --> 00:17:32.273
A fighter has to attack
his rival's sensors

00:17:32.351 --> 00:17:33.841
without exposing his own.

00:17:33.919 --> 00:17:36.080
Are you two going to talk
or you here to watch?

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:14.491
He looks like he could
pick up a shuttlecraft.

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.652
He's a Pendari.

00:18:15.727 --> 00:18:17.718
They're known for
their superior strength.

00:18:17.796 --> 00:18:18.728
And their bad temper.

00:18:18.797 --> 00:18:20.196
I hear they have a tendency

00:18:20.265 --> 00:18:22.392
to throw their opponents
into the stands.

00:18:22.468 --> 00:18:23.833
Be ready to duck.

00:18:40.352 --> 00:18:42.149
Seven?

00:18:54.199 --> 00:18:56.064
Seven!

00:18:56.135 --> 00:18:57.602
Seven!

00:18:59.505 --> 00:19:01.769
You're no bigger than
a Tarkanian field mouse.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:06.209
Penk's insulting me by putting
you in the pit to face me.

00:19:06.278 --> 00:19:08.769
I must warn you,
I possess superior strength.

00:19:08.847 --> 00:19:10.940
I'm trembling.

00:19:15.554 --> 00:19:17.579
Seven!

00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:19.715
Seven!

00:19:19.791 --> 00:19:21.190
Seven!

00:19:22.594 --> 00:19:25.529
I assure you,
resistance is futile.

00:19:25.597 --> 00:19:27.531
So is all your talk.

00:19:31.603 --> 00:19:32.592
Seven!

00:19:32.671 --> 00:19:34.901
It's no use.
She can't hear us.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.905
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:19:37.009 --> 00:19:38.033
Come in.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.203
Calling to give me
a blow-by-blow description

00:19:40.279 --> 00:19:41.268
of the match, Commander?

00:19:41.346 --> 00:19:43.075
Seven of Nine is in the pit.

00:19:43.148 --> 00:19:44.080
What?

00:19:44.149 --> 00:19:45.081
No time to explain.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.242
Beam her out of there!

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.690
I have no desire to
inflict further damage.

00:20:00.766 --> 00:20:02.700
I'm afraid I can't say the same.

00:20:12.511 --> 00:20:14.376
I'm locked onto
the coordinates of the pit.

00:20:14.446 --> 00:20:15.413
Seven's not there.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.640
I'm looking right at her!

00:20:16.715 --> 00:20:18.478
Not according to these sensors.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.484
Maybe their life signs
are masked.

00:20:20.552 --> 00:20:22.918
Try recalibrating
the bio-scanners.

00:20:22.988 --> 00:20:24.717
Acknowledged.

00:20:27.192 --> 00:20:28.921
There's nothing to lock on to.

00:20:28.994 --> 00:20:31.656
The only readings I'm picking up
are photonic.

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:32.662
Holograms?

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.096
They're transmitting the fight

00:20:34.166 --> 00:20:35.224
from another location.

00:20:58.824 --> 00:21:01.486
Transmission to one of
the arenas on Norcadia Prime

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.391
is being disrupted.

00:21:03.462 --> 00:21:04.895
Compensate.

00:21:29.688 --> 00:21:31.155
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:21:31.223 --> 00:21:34.056
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:21:34.126 --> 00:21:37.721
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:21:37.796 --> 00:21:38.956
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:21:39.064 --> 00:21:42.761
Voyager, four to beam up.

00:21:47.506 --> 00:21:49.701
We've scanned
the Norcadian surface, Captain.

00:21:49.775 --> 00:21:50.969
There's no sign of them.

00:21:51.043 --> 00:21:52.635
Any luck
tracing the transmission?

00:21:52.711 --> 00:21:54.611
We're trying, but it's not easy.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.612
There are transmissions

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:57.273
being sent to every
planet in the sector.

00:21:57.349 --> 00:22:00.216
I guess you aren't the only ones
who enjoy this sport.

00:22:00.285 --> 00:22:01.912
It could take days
before we can figure out

00:22:01.987 --> 00:22:03.386
where Seven and Tuvok
are being held.

00:22:03.455 --> 00:22:04.786
What about diplomatic channels?

00:22:04.856 --> 00:22:07.290
Neelix is meeting with a group
of Norcadian officials.

00:22:07.359 --> 00:22:09.486
Well, let's hope he gets
their cooperation.

00:22:09.561 --> 00:22:11.426
When can we
expect you back?

00:22:11.496 --> 00:22:13.657
I'm at the outer rim
of the Pendari system.

00:22:13.732 --> 00:22:15.097
At best, I'm 48 hours away.

00:22:15.167 --> 00:22:17.533
Sorry to cut your
vacation short.

00:22:17.602 --> 00:22:19.297
That's okay, Commander.

00:22:19.371 --> 00:22:21.100
Keep me informed. Janeway out.

00:22:33.118 --> 00:22:34.847
Stay away from me.

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:37.354
It's a dermal regenerator.

00:22:37.422 --> 00:22:39.913
The Pendari you
fought injured you.

00:22:39.991 --> 00:22:40.958
Now, keep still.

00:22:41.026 --> 00:22:42.960
It's almost out of power.

00:22:43.061 --> 00:22:45.586
I'd prefer that you use it
to treat Commander Tuvok.

00:22:45.664 --> 00:22:46.756
I already have.

00:22:46.832 --> 00:22:48.823
He's sleeping.

00:22:50.335 --> 00:22:51.768
Why are you helping us?

00:22:51.837 --> 00:22:55.432
I recognize fellow hunters
when I see them.

00:22:55.507 --> 00:22:56.940
I'm no hunter.

00:22:59.411 --> 00:23:01.845
I saw your match today.

00:23:01.913 --> 00:23:03.904
Your skills are impressive.

00:23:04.049 --> 00:23:07.109
The Pendari would disagree.

00:23:07.185 --> 00:23:10.086
You almost defeated him,
but at the last moment,

00:23:10.155 --> 00:23:11.247
you hesitated.

00:23:11.323 --> 00:23:13.086
You... questioned
your desire

00:23:13.158 --> 00:23:15.092
to destroy your prey.

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:17.754
I have no such desire.

00:23:17.829 --> 00:23:20.730
Don't you?

00:23:20.799 --> 00:23:23.290
I thought I saw it in your eyes.

00:23:23.368 --> 00:23:25.632
With the proper training,

00:23:25.704 --> 00:23:27.433
you could become a champion.

00:23:27.506 --> 00:23:29.565
Until our ship comes
to rescue us,

00:23:29.641 --> 00:23:31.336
my only goal is to survive.

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:34.538
Do you know the difference

00:23:34.613 --> 00:23:38.879
between a survivor
and a champion here?

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.884
There isn't one.

00:23:45.891 --> 00:23:49.156
I wanted to be the first
to congratulate you.

00:23:49.227 --> 00:23:50.717
I lost.

00:23:50.796 --> 00:23:52.127
Exactly.

00:23:52.197 --> 00:23:54.961
There's a great deal
of hostility toward the Borg

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:56.533
in this sector.

00:23:56.601 --> 00:23:59.866
Whenever the Pendari landed
a blow, our audience grew.

00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:03.305
We're getting
tens of thousands of requests

00:24:03.375 --> 00:24:05.036
to see you fight again.

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:06.702
She needs time
to recuperate...

00:24:06.778 --> 00:24:09.872
to prepare for her next bout.

00:24:09.948 --> 00:24:11.438
I agree.

00:24:11.516 --> 00:24:14.110
There's a Red Match scheduled
for the day after tomorrow.

00:24:14.186 --> 00:24:15.847
The Pendari
was supposed to compete,

00:24:15.921 --> 00:24:17.616
but I've entered
you in his place.

00:24:21.359 --> 00:24:25.853
If three billion people paid
to see you hurt,

00:24:25.931 --> 00:24:29.162
imagine how many will pay
to see you die.

00:24:34.306 --> 00:24:37.503
Survival may be more difficult
than I imagined.

00:24:37.576 --> 00:24:40.204
You will win the match.

00:24:40.278 --> 00:24:41.939
What makes you say that?

00:24:42.080 --> 00:24:45.538
I know your opponent;
I know his weaknesses.

00:24:45.617 --> 00:24:48.051
I can train you to defeat him.

00:24:48.119 --> 00:24:51.282
I told you, I will not kill
anyone in that arena.

00:24:51.356 --> 00:24:53.654
Consider the alternative.

00:25:08.139 --> 00:25:09.606
Teach me.

00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:20.781
You're letting
your elbow fall,

00:25:20.852 --> 00:25:22.547
exposing your target.

00:25:22.621 --> 00:25:23.553
You're mistaken.

00:25:23.622 --> 00:25:25.453
My arm is positioned properly.

00:25:25.524 --> 00:25:27.014
"When executing
the Tanyk Defense,

00:25:27.092 --> 00:25:28.559
"the blocking elbow must remain

00:25:28.627 --> 00:25:30.185
parallel
to the median sensor."

00:25:30.262 --> 00:25:31.752
Ah, the Book of Tsunkatse.

00:25:31.830 --> 00:25:34.128
Commander Tuvok borrowed it
from one of the other fighters.

00:25:34.199 --> 00:25:37.225
It is obvious
you've studied it well.

00:25:37.302 --> 00:25:38.769
I'm attempting to perfect
a defense against...

00:25:41.973 --> 00:25:43.736
That was not one

00:25:43.808 --> 00:25:45.400
of the 33
sanctioned maneuvers.

00:25:45.477 --> 00:25:47.308
There must be 34.

00:25:47.379 --> 00:25:49.779
I was unprepared
for your attack.

00:25:49.848 --> 00:25:52.146
Is that what you're going to say
to your opponent?

00:25:52.217 --> 00:25:54.708
Stop thinking like a drone.

00:25:54.786 --> 00:25:56.083
Sanctioned maneuvers,

00:25:56.154 --> 00:25:57.951
perfecting defenses.

00:25:58.023 --> 00:26:01.390
You cannot assimilate Tsunkatse
from a book.

00:26:01.459 --> 00:26:04.087
You must live it, feel it.

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:07.292
In here.

00:26:07.365 --> 00:26:09.731
Your movements

00:26:09.801 --> 00:26:12.235
must become instinct.

00:26:12.304 --> 00:26:15.535
An attack could come at any time
from any direction.

00:26:15.607 --> 00:26:18.576
You must learn to improvise.

00:26:18.643 --> 00:26:19.701
Like this?

00:26:21.479 --> 00:26:24.676
I've observed you often favor
your left side.

00:26:24.749 --> 00:26:27.513
Very perceptive.

00:26:27.586 --> 00:26:31.283
It's a wound I sustained
in one of my first matches.

00:26:31.356 --> 00:26:34.757
After 19 years,
it still hasn't healed properly.

00:26:37.195 --> 00:26:39.322
You've been here a long time.

00:26:39.397 --> 00:26:44.767
I was taken during
my son's first hunt.

00:26:44.836 --> 00:26:47.930
He was so proud
to be with his father.

00:26:48.039 --> 00:26:50.940
Watching every
movement I made,

00:26:51.076 --> 00:26:52.566
imitating my gestures.

00:26:52.644 --> 00:26:54.942
But instead of bringing
home his first trophy,

00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:59.107
he saw his father become
someone else's prey.

00:26:59.184 --> 00:27:00.811
Do you know
what happened to him?

00:27:00.885 --> 00:27:04.082
I never saw him again.

00:27:04.155 --> 00:27:05.816
All Penk would say

00:27:05.890 --> 00:27:10.327
was that the boy was
too small for competition.

00:27:10.395 --> 00:27:13.489
Perhaps he managed
to return home.

00:27:16.501 --> 00:27:18.128
You let down your defenses.

00:27:18.203 --> 00:27:19.397
Why?

00:27:19.471 --> 00:27:21.132
- I was...
- What?

00:27:21.206 --> 00:27:22.867
Feeling sorry for me?

00:27:22.941 --> 00:27:24.101
My tragic past?

00:27:24.175 --> 00:27:25.164
Yes.

00:27:25.243 --> 00:27:27.734
You must never sympathize

00:27:27.812 --> 00:27:28.904
with your prey.

00:27:29.047 --> 00:27:30.708
Unless you accept that,

00:27:30.782 --> 00:27:33.683
you will die.

00:27:36.688 --> 00:27:38.155
We'll continue.

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:04.248
How did it go?

00:28:04.315 --> 00:28:05.680
Oh, the Norcadians

00:28:05.750 --> 00:28:08.116
were shocked to learn
that off-worlders might be

00:28:08.186 --> 00:28:09.813
participating against
their will.

00:28:09.888 --> 00:28:11.651
Uh, the Ambassador
promised to begin

00:28:11.723 --> 00:28:12.781
an immediate investigation.

00:28:12.857 --> 00:28:14.518
You don't sound too convinced.

00:28:14.592 --> 00:28:15.650
I'm not.

00:28:15.727 --> 00:28:17.854
I spoke to one
of the Pendari delegates.

00:28:17.929 --> 00:28:19.021
According to him,

00:28:19.097 --> 00:28:20.758
a huge percentage
of the planet's revenue

00:28:20.832 --> 00:28:23.164
is derived from Tsunkatse.

00:28:23.234 --> 00:28:24.360
Nobody wants to do anything

00:28:24.436 --> 00:28:26.028
that might interfere
with the game.

00:28:26.104 --> 00:28:27.036
So they turn a blind eye

00:28:27.105 --> 00:28:28.163
to the recruitment tactics.

00:28:28.239 --> 00:28:29.706
We're not going to get any help

00:28:29.774 --> 00:28:31.036
through official channels.

00:28:31.109 --> 00:28:33.669
It's hard to believe
a-a-a civilization

00:28:33.745 --> 00:28:35.713
whose favorite pastime
is cheering

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:37.907
while innocent people
fight each other.

00:28:38.049 --> 00:28:39.880
If Seven and Tuvok
hadn't been abducted,

00:28:39.951 --> 00:28:42.818
we might still
be cheering, too.

00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:50.925
What have you got?

00:28:50.995 --> 00:28:53.122
Well, one of the reasons
we were having trouble

00:28:53.198 --> 00:28:55.257
isolating the source
of the transmissions

00:28:55.333 --> 00:28:57.426
was because they never
seem to be coming

00:28:57.502 --> 00:28:58.833
from the same place twice.

00:28:58.903 --> 00:29:00.598
At first, we thought
the matches were

00:29:00.672 --> 00:29:02.162
being held in
various locations.

00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:04.606
But when we
connected the dots,

00:29:04.676 --> 00:29:07.509
we realized the pattern
conformed to a flight path.

00:29:07.579 --> 00:29:09.479
One that spanned
the entire sector.

00:29:09.547 --> 00:29:11.981
They're transmitting
the fights from a ship.

00:29:12.050 --> 00:29:14.018
Like a traveling carnival.

00:29:14.085 --> 00:29:15.552
Oh, this is no carnival.

00:29:15.620 --> 00:29:17.019
Five million metric tons,

00:29:17.088 --> 00:29:18.612
reinforced hull plating

00:29:18.690 --> 00:29:20.521
protected
by covariant shielding,

00:29:20.592 --> 00:29:22.355
neutronic weaponry.

00:29:22.427 --> 00:29:24.861
It's way out
of our weight class.

00:29:24.929 --> 00:29:26.692
The bigger they come,
Lieutenant.

00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:28.630
Transmit these coordinates
to the Captain.

00:29:28.700 --> 00:29:30.600
Tell her we could use a hand.

00:29:58.229 --> 00:29:59.696
Excellent.

00:29:59.764 --> 00:30:01.391
When your opponent
enters the arena,

00:30:01.466 --> 00:30:02.728
what do you see?

00:30:02.801 --> 00:30:03.893
My prey.

00:30:03.968 --> 00:30:05.902
And what do you do to your prey?

00:30:05.970 --> 00:30:08.530
Hunt it down and kill it.

00:30:12.911 --> 00:30:15.277
Go rest before your match.

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:23.951
Thank you.

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:26.546
Thank me...

00:30:26.624 --> 00:30:29.092
by winning.

00:30:34.399 --> 00:30:37.960
Penk's guards are making
their inspection rounds.

00:30:38.036 --> 00:30:39.401
Progress?

00:30:39.470 --> 00:30:41.870
Both the dampening field
and the shielding

00:30:41.940 --> 00:30:43.805
of this vessel
are tetryon-based.

00:30:43.875 --> 00:30:45.934
But without access to
the control interface,

00:30:46.010 --> 00:30:48.410
I can't disable either.

00:30:48.479 --> 00:30:50.071
Your training?

00:30:50.148 --> 00:30:51.615
Complete.

00:30:51.683 --> 00:30:55.244
Are you adequately prepared?

00:30:55.320 --> 00:30:57.481
The Hirogen
is an efficient instructor.

00:30:57.555 --> 00:30:58.988
He believes I'll win.

00:30:59.123 --> 00:31:01.250
That troubles you.

00:31:01.326 --> 00:31:03.385
The idea of killing someone

00:31:03.461 --> 00:31:05.691
for the entertainment
of others is detestable.

00:31:05.763 --> 00:31:08.732
Is the idea
of losing your own life

00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:10.859
for the entertainment of others
more palatable?

00:31:10.935 --> 00:31:12.869
As a drone,

00:31:12.937 --> 00:31:14.461
you took many lives.

00:31:14.539 --> 00:31:16.734
I was acting as part
of the collective.

00:31:16.808 --> 00:31:19.538
You're worried
you won't have the strength

00:31:19.611 --> 00:31:21.875
to accomplish the task
on your own.

00:31:21.946 --> 00:31:25.006
I'm worried that I will.

00:31:34.459 --> 00:31:36.256
It's time.

00:31:41.666 --> 00:31:45.796
Do whatever it takes
to survive.

00:33:04.248 --> 00:33:06.011
You knew.

00:33:06.084 --> 00:33:07.813
Yes.

00:33:11.022 --> 00:33:12.819
Training me was a deception.

00:33:12.890 --> 00:33:15.552
You wished to familiarize
yourself with my weaknesses.

00:33:15.626 --> 00:33:18.891
I was helping you
to overcome them.

00:33:18.963 --> 00:33:19.895
Why?

00:33:21.733 --> 00:33:25.169
19 years is a long time.

00:33:25.236 --> 00:33:26.669
I've grown tired.

00:33:26.738 --> 00:33:29.070
You wish to be killed
in the arena.

00:33:29.140 --> 00:33:31.938
I want a death my son

00:33:32.043 --> 00:33:33.169
would be proud of.

00:33:33.244 --> 00:33:35.303
I won't be the one
to provide it.

00:33:37.048 --> 00:33:39.915
Then I'll be forced
to kill you.

00:33:39.984 --> 00:33:40.973
Ya!

00:33:52.563 --> 00:33:53.860
Approaching the vessel.

00:33:53.931 --> 00:33:54.955
Take us out of warp.

00:33:55.099 --> 00:33:56.896
Raise shields
and charge weapons.

00:33:56.968 --> 00:33:58.526
Any sign of Tuvok and Seven?

00:33:58.603 --> 00:34:01.163
Our sensors can't penetrate
their shields.

00:34:01.239 --> 00:34:02.968
Hail them.

00:34:05.543 --> 00:34:08.034
This is not a convenient time.

00:34:08.112 --> 00:34:10.580
I'm Commander Chakotay
of the Starship Voyager.

00:34:10.648 --> 00:34:12.309
You're holding
two of my people.

00:34:12.383 --> 00:34:14.442
You'll have to be more specific.

00:34:14.519 --> 00:34:17.147
Commander Tuvok
and Seven of Nine.

00:34:17.221 --> 00:34:18.483
Return them, now.

00:34:18.556 --> 00:34:20.581
The Borg drone and her friend.

00:34:20.658 --> 00:34:23.354
I'm afraid
she's occupied at the moment.

00:34:23.428 --> 00:34:25.726
You have 30 seconds
before I open fire.

00:34:27.331 --> 00:34:28.764
A fighter.

00:34:28.833 --> 00:34:32.325
I respect that,
but you're no match for me.

00:34:45.416 --> 00:34:47.782
We can still find
another way out of this.

00:34:47.852 --> 00:34:49.649
There is no other way.

00:34:50.588 --> 00:34:51.850
You're still

00:34:51.923 --> 00:34:53.618
dropping your elbow.

00:34:57.628 --> 00:35:00.995
Make a choice,
hunter or prey?

00:35:03.468 --> 00:35:05.595
Hunter or prey?

00:35:27.191 --> 00:35:29.819
Direct hit to their
aft shield generators.

00:35:29.894 --> 00:35:30.883
Still no sign of Seven,

00:35:30.962 --> 00:35:32.122
but I've got a lock on Tuvok.

00:35:32.196 --> 00:35:33.288
Beam him to Sick Bay.

00:35:33.364 --> 00:35:34.388
Keep targeting

00:35:34.465 --> 00:35:36.330
those generators.

00:35:36.400 --> 00:35:38.061
Transport complete.

00:35:38.136 --> 00:35:39.160
Bridge to Tuvok.

00:35:39.237 --> 00:35:40.534
Go ahead, Commander.

00:35:40.605 --> 00:35:42.402
Do you know Seven's status?

00:35:42.473 --> 00:35:45.931
She's being forced to fight...
to the death.

00:35:46.043 --> 00:35:48.409
I believe
they're on the uppermost deck.

00:35:48.479 --> 00:35:50.606
That section's protected
by multiphasic force fields.

00:35:50.681 --> 00:35:51.648
I can't penetrate them.

00:35:54.519 --> 00:35:56.214
Shields down to 40 percent.

00:35:57.188 --> 00:35:59.418
32 percent.

00:36:01.859 --> 00:36:03.383
You're getting weak.

00:36:04.395 --> 00:36:06.488
I should have found
worthier prey.

00:36:12.870 --> 00:36:16.203
You're imperfect.

00:36:23.781 --> 00:36:25.806
Is that the best you can do?

00:36:35.793 --> 00:36:37.317
Shields are down.

00:36:37.395 --> 00:36:39.363
Evasive maneuvers.

00:36:39.430 --> 00:36:40.397
Harry?

00:36:40.464 --> 00:36:41.431
Still can't get a lock.

00:36:41.499 --> 00:36:42.693
Should I get us out of here

00:36:42.767 --> 00:36:44.394
before they knock out
our propulsion?

00:36:44.468 --> 00:36:45.435
Not yet.

00:36:45.503 --> 00:36:46.697
If we can't beam her out,

00:36:46.771 --> 00:36:48.500
maybe we can shut down
the transmission.

00:36:48.573 --> 00:36:50.905
If nobody's watching,
then why continue the fight?

00:36:50.975 --> 00:36:52.840
Start targeting
their signal generators.

00:36:52.910 --> 00:36:55.071
Hull breach on Deck 11.

00:36:55.146 --> 00:36:56.078
Seal it.

00:37:02.420 --> 00:37:05.048
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:37:06.157 --> 00:37:07.852
We've lost weapons.

00:37:07.925 --> 00:37:10.291
Another vessel is approaching.

00:37:10.361 --> 00:37:12.386
Great. Now they're
bringing in reinforcements.

00:37:12.463 --> 00:37:13.862
No, this one's on our side.

00:37:13.931 --> 00:37:15.660
It's the Delta Flyer.

00:37:22.573 --> 00:37:24.302
Good to see you, Captain.

00:37:24.375 --> 00:37:27.242
Nothing like getting back
to work after a long vacation.

00:37:27.311 --> 00:37:29.677
We need you to target
their signal generators.

00:37:29.747 --> 00:37:31.112
Understood.

00:37:46.764 --> 00:37:49.699
We've lost more
than half our audience.

00:37:49.767 --> 00:37:53.032
Reroute power
to Transmitters 5 and 6.

00:37:53.104 --> 00:37:55.334
They've reduced power
to their force fields.

00:37:55.406 --> 00:37:57.101
I've got two life
signs in there...

00:37:57.174 --> 00:37:58.198
Seven and a Hirogen...

00:37:58.276 --> 00:38:00.039
but I can't get
an individual lock.

00:38:00.111 --> 00:38:02.045
Transport them both
if you have to.

00:38:02.113 --> 00:38:03.045
Tom.

00:38:03.114 --> 00:38:05.082
Aye, sir.

00:38:24.201 --> 00:38:26.362
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:38:26.437 --> 00:38:30.601
Tsunkat! Tsunkat! Tsunkat!
Tsunkat! Tsunkat!

00:38:33.144 --> 00:38:37.080
Never... let your prey suffer.

00:38:37.148 --> 00:38:38.615
Kill it.

00:38:48.659 --> 00:38:50.684
Seven, stand away.

00:38:52.430 --> 00:38:54.364
It's all right.

00:38:56.967 --> 00:38:58.730
This fight is over.

00:39:15.219 --> 00:39:19.121
Captain's Log, Stardate 53529.4.

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:21.886
We've resumed course
for the Alpha Quadrant

00:39:21.992 --> 00:39:23.391
and initiated repairs.

00:39:23.461 --> 00:39:24.826
I can't say I'm sorry

00:39:24.895 --> 00:39:27.386
to see this shore leave
come to an end.

00:39:27.465 --> 00:39:29.456
We've located
an Hirogen hunting party

00:39:29.533 --> 00:39:30.727
three light-years away.

00:39:30.801 --> 00:39:32.769
They've agreed
to rendezvous with us.

00:39:32.837 --> 00:39:34.668
I'm grateful.

00:39:39.110 --> 00:39:41.340
Would you excuse us?

00:39:42.380 --> 00:39:43.506
Very well,

00:39:43.581 --> 00:39:45.913
but if you should
need anything...

00:39:46.050 --> 00:39:48.780
an analgesic,
a phaser rifle...

00:39:50.388 --> 00:39:52.549
...don't hesitate to ask.

00:39:55.426 --> 00:39:57.087
I apologize for the Doctor.

00:39:57.161 --> 00:40:00.824
He's very protective of me.

00:40:00.898 --> 00:40:04.925
He doesn't realize how
well you defend yourself.

00:40:09.707 --> 00:40:11.470
A trophy.

00:40:16.547 --> 00:40:19.516
What will you do now,
search for new prey?

00:40:19.583 --> 00:40:24.953
No, this time I will be
searching for my son.

00:40:25.089 --> 00:40:27.114
If he is as clever
as his father,

00:40:27.191 --> 00:40:29.159
he may be difficult to locate.

00:40:29.226 --> 00:40:31.660
I've been wondering.

00:40:33.664 --> 00:40:36.360
Would you have killed me?

00:40:42.573 --> 00:40:44.473
I don't know.

00:40:44.542 --> 00:40:47.602
Ah...

00:40:47.678 --> 00:40:50.146
Fortunately, you were right.

00:40:50.214 --> 00:40:52.546
There was another way out.

00:41:03.727 --> 00:41:06.924
I thought you might
require assistance.

00:41:07.064 --> 00:41:09.123
Thank you.

00:41:18.876 --> 00:41:23.540
I realize we share an
affinity for silences,

00:41:23.614 --> 00:41:26.105
but in this instance...

00:41:26.183 --> 00:41:28.947
I feel compelled to speak.

00:41:29.019 --> 00:41:32.147
If you hadn't offered
to take my place in the arena,

00:41:32.223 --> 00:41:34.487
it's likely I would have
been killed.

00:41:34.558 --> 00:41:37.823
I made the logical choice,
as you would have.

00:41:37.895 --> 00:41:40.921
Still, I owe you
a debt of gratitude.

00:41:40.998 --> 00:41:42.431
Assisting me

00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:46.834
with these recalibrations
will be sufficient thanks.

00:41:46.904 --> 00:41:48.929
Have you fully recovered?

00:41:49.006 --> 00:41:51.201
I'm experiencing minor pain

00:41:51.275 --> 00:41:53.641
beneath my occipital implant,

00:41:53.711 --> 00:41:57.078
but the Doctor believes
it is temporary.

00:41:57.147 --> 00:42:00.275
I wasn't referring to
your physical condition.

00:42:05.589 --> 00:42:10.151
When the Hirogen referred
to me as weak,

00:42:10.227 --> 00:42:12.024
he was correct.

00:42:13.898 --> 00:42:15.763
But you overpowered him.

00:42:15.833 --> 00:42:17.630
Because I lost control.

00:42:17.701 --> 00:42:19.532
Given the circumstances,

00:42:19.603 --> 00:42:21.935
your behavior
was understandable.

00:42:22.072 --> 00:42:24.540
I've spent the last three years

00:42:24.608 --> 00:42:26.974
struggling to regain
my humanity.

00:42:28.646 --> 00:42:31.547
I'm afraid I may have
lost it again in that arena.

00:42:31.615 --> 00:42:34.948
You're experiencing
difficult emotions.

00:42:35.019 --> 00:42:36.486
Guilt...

00:42:36.554 --> 00:42:37.816
shame...

00:42:37.888 --> 00:42:39.150
remorse.

00:42:39.223 --> 00:42:43.592
Then you haven't lost
your humanity.

00:42:43.661 --> 00:42:46.562
You have reaffirmed it.
